WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:12.360
Today we are going to see how ChatGPT just&nbsp;
got supercharged. Normally, this is OpenAI’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:18.000
chat assistant, where we get a little text&nbsp;
box, enter our questions as a text prompt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.740
and it shall answer. However, get this, today,&nbsp;
we don’t even need to prompt ChatGPT anymore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:33.900
because, and now, hold on to your papers,&nbsp;
because it can prompt itself. What? How?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:40.740
That sounds insane. But yes, all that&nbsp;
is true. We can describe a complex task,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:48.420
and it will by itself break it down into smaller&nbsp;
steps. And it also does them all! For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:55.560
here it is asked to buy a pair of AirPods,&nbsp;
and as you see, it knows that it first has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:01.980
to search for it, look for deals, yes, we&nbsp;
got one. It is indeed on the right track,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:10.320
and then, gets distracted by a privacy policy.&nbsp;
Or perhaps it knows something we don’t know yet.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:17.460
Yes, this is a version of ChatGPT that&nbsp;
can make decisions and take action. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.960
what can we use this for?

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:24.840
Well, we can even ask it to build&nbsp;
a website for us. And it adds the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:28.020
required goodies, step by step. Really cool!

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:35.040
Now, this is Two Minute Papers, so we&nbsp;
want to give it a scholarly task. Oh yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:42.060
let’s ask it to research itself. That is one&nbsp;
more task with several steps involved. And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:50.220
yes, this interface gives us a little opportunity&nbsp;
to pop the hood and hear its thoughts. It first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:57.300
wants to search for AutoGPT, browse around a&nbsp;
little, and finally create an outline about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:04.200
itself for us. Once again, the key part is&nbsp;
that it can take a complex task, and break it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:13.500
into small steps. That is incredible. It also&nbsp;
reminds itself to not wander around too much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:21.180
if it finds a tasty privacy policy, and focus on&nbsp;
the main task instead. Good thinking, little AI!

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:25.320
Now let’s see what happens&nbsp;
then…the search takes place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:32.640
we get a ton of results, and finally,&nbsp;
it enters GitHub, the home of AutoGPT,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:39.600
we see how it reads through the page,&nbsp;
and finally, we get our answer. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:45.720
my first question was, is this a copy-paste&nbsp;
from the website, or did it really read the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:53.940
whole thing and distill down the information into&nbsp;
one paragraph? Yes it did, good job, little AI!

00:02:53.940 --> 00:03:01.500
So, at this point, my question was, what is&nbsp;
AutoGPT? What role could this play in our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:08.340
lives? And, have a look at this. We can also get&nbsp;
a progress report where it tells us what it has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:17.220
done, and what there is left to be done. So, yes,&nbsp;
AutoGPT feels very much like a team of assistants.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:24.960
The first version of OpenAI’s ChatGPT is barely a&nbsp;
few months old, and it can already prompt itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:32.640
chain prompts together, and report back to us&nbsp;
on where exactly it is. That is incredible.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:39.060
And we can even ask it to have a look at&nbsp;
a piece of computer code. Then, it again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:45.240
breaks down the task into small pieces.&nbsp;
Evaluation, improvement, and finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:51.420
testing. And it does all of that.&nbsp;
Like a team of assistants would. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:58.920
this is a computer that kind of fixes itself.&nbsp;
How cool is that? What a time to be alive!

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:04.980
Now, a few more things that you should&nbsp;
know about this. One, by default, it asks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:11.580
for permission before each step. That is a good&nbsp;
idea. Two, these are just the first few steps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:17.220
and when you start using it, you will find&nbsp;
that it is a bit slow, a bit expensive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:23.640
and quite limited. Also, I would like to&nbsp;
make sure not to overstate what AutoGPT&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:29.940
can do at the moment, however, can you even&nbsp;
imagine what this will be able to do just two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:34.500
more papers down the line? If you have some&nbsp;
ideas, let me know in the comments below.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:40.500
So, do you wish to try it? Can you?&nbsp;
Yes you can! You can run it locally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:45.780
or even try it on the web. I’ve&nbsp;
included both links in the video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:50.040
description. Note that you will&nbsp;
need an API key to perform that.

